        "id": "7d3b8c908bf32b2ca0e8943280aa509f92cf1d1c",
        "tree_id": "a24e0c2559ddf4448639b5d49db1bf178cdffef4",
        "message": "fix(1): move OcrEngine into the feature module; it is not compilable in :app\n\n    Unresolved reference 'SplitInstallStateUpdateListener'.\n    Unresolved reference 'SplitInstallState'.\n    Unresolved reference 'getInstalledModuleNames'.\n    Unresolved reference 'uninstallModule'.\n    Argument type mismatch: actual type is\n      'com.grapsee.gsai.ocr.<anonymous>', but\n      'com.google.android.play.core.splitinstall.SplitInstallStateUpdateListener'\n      was expected\n\nPlay Core was not resolving onto the :app compile classpath. The code belongs in\nthe feature module anyway, and the app module should never link against the\nfallback's types: it asks the module whether it is installed and nothing more.\nA reference from :app to a dynamic feature's classes is an architecture error\nregardless of whether it happens to compile.",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-28T08:18:42Z",
